steps:
  - text: |
      {[ht,$start]&thinsp;Open EM&bull;Scope}

      The previous tour examined energy consumption by way of **Joulescope Viewer** screenshots of raw power captures.

      We’ll now explore the _same_ captures with **EM&bull;Scope**, en&shy;abling more systematic measurement and comparison.

      While you'll continue &ldquo;watching screenshots&rdquo;, we encour&shy;age you to explore **EM&bull;Scope** at each stop.

      To that end, click **Open EM&bull;Scope** on the **EM&bull;Home** page and keep its tab handy as you advance through the tour.

      <div class="em-info">

      You should also follow the link to **Download Joulescope Viewer** in preparation for what follows.

      </div>

  - cmds:
      - view 1
    text: |
      {[ht,checklist]&thinsp;Explore the Captures}

      When initially launched, **EM&bull;Scope** displays a pre-popu&shy;lated list of _captures_ found in its default home folder {[dc,1]}&thinsp;.

      <div class="em-info">

      Buttons to the right enable you to select other capture folders, as well as to operate on the current captures.

      </div>

      Each row in the table (sorted here by **Capture** {[dc,2]} name) shows measurements and scores computed for this entry.

      Besides its familiar **Sleep&thinsp;&mu;A** and **Event&thinsp;&mu;J** measurements, each capture entry receives a pair of **EM&bull;eralds** {[dc,3]} scores.

      Before explaining **EM&bull;eralds**, let's click the last icon {[dc,4]} on the `nrf52` entry to view this capture's waveform&thinsp;&hellip;

  - cmds:
      - view 2
    text: |
      {[ht,monitor_heart]&thinsp;Inspect the Waveform}

  - cmds:
      - view 3
    text: |
      {[ht,electric_bolt]&thinsp;EM&bull;eralds}

  - cmds:
      - view 4
    text: |
      {[ht,timeline]&thinsp;Rescan a Capture}

  - cmds:
      - view 5
    text: |
      {[ht,$extra]&thinsp;Extra Credit}

      {[bi,task_alt]} TODO

      {[bi,task_alt]} TODO

      {[bi,task_alt]} TODO

  - cmds:
      - open 6
    text: |
      {[ht,$steps]&thinsp;Next Steps}

      {[hc]}
